    "alert_id": "EX4_001",
    "title": "Carbamazepine-DTG interaction lowers DTG levels",
    "message": "Guidelines state carbamazepine decreases DTG levels by 30–70% and recommend using valproic acid instead. Patient started carbamazepine 2 weeks ago while on DTG-based TLD. Viral load rose from <50 copies/mL (Sep 2025) to 1,240 copies/mL today, with adherence reported good. This temporal relationship strongly suggests the interaction caused subtherapeutic DTG levels leading to virologic breakthrough. The patient is already on valproate, which the guidelines specifically recommend as the alternative antiepileptic. Carbamazepine toxicity (level 14 mcg/mL, hyponatremia, ataxia, nystagmus) provides further reason to discontinue it.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Stop carbamazepine and manage seizures with valproate monotherapy as guidelines recommend. Repeat viral load after discontinuation to assess DTG level recovery.",
