    "title": "Detectable viral load requires enhanced adherence counseling",
    "message": "Guidelines define treatment failure as two consecutive viral load results >1,000 copies/mL. For high-level viremia ≥1,000, guidelines require intensive adherence counseling (IAC) with 3 sessions scoring >95%, CD4 testing, and repeat viral load using two plasma samples. If repeat remains ≥1,000, HIV drug resistance testing and regimen switching are indicated. Patient's viral load is 1,240 copies/mL today, up from <50 in September 2025. The clinician's plan does not mention IAC, CD4 testing, or repeat VL protocol. The likely cause is the carbamazepine-DTG interaction, but the full guideline workup should still be initiated.",
    "issue_type": "guideline_deviation",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Initiate IAC sessions, conduct CD4 testing, and repeat viral load with two plasma samples. If still ≥1,000, perform HIV drug resistance testing and consider regimen switch.",
