    "alert_id": "EX4_003",
    "title": "Carbamazepine toxicity with hyponatremia",
    "message": "Patient has carbamazepine level 14 mcg/mL (therapeutic 4–12), with clinical features of toxicity including ataxia, horizontal nystagmus, fine tremor, dizziness, and headaches. Hyponatremia (sodium 128 mmol/L) is also present and is a known adverse effect of carbamazepine. ALT 68 U/L may reflect hepatic effects of carbamazepine, valproate, or both antiepileptics together. The clinician plans dose reduction, but given the concurrent DTG interaction and the guideline recommendation to use valproic acid instead, simply reducing the dose may not address the underlying interaction driving virologic failure.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
