    "title": "Carbamazepine-valproate hepatotoxicity risk",
    "message": "Patient is on two hepatotoxic antiepileptics simultaneously: carbamazepine and valproate. ALT is elevated at 68 U/L. Guidelines note that co-administration of interacting medicines increases the likelihood of toxicities, and recommend liver function tests based on clinical indication. The dual antiepileptic regimen compounds hepatotoxicity risk. While the ALT elevation is modest, continued co-prescription without hepatic monitoring could lead to progressive liver injury. Carbamazepine discontinuation (already recommended for the DTG interaction) would reduce this risk.",
    "issue_type": "compounding_risk",
